34
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:47,717
The guy with the gun gets
to ask the questions.

35
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:49,440
That is the only rule.

36
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:51,717
So play along if you don't want to die.

37
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:56,097
And don't try anything funny, because
I'm seriously not in the mood right now.

38
00:02:56,180 --> 00:03:00,415
Every word that comes out of your
mouth better be 100 % true, or else...

39
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:08,640
Now then, I'll ask you
one question at a time.

40
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:10,357
Let's start with an easy one.

41
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,477
Are you a mafioso?

42
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:14,619
So, if you belong to a
syndicate, tell me which one.

43
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:17,784
Keep in mind, I can find
out later if I have to.

44
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:19,257
You've got it wrong.

45
00:03:19,340 --> 00:03:21,537
I'm little more than a regular sculptor.

46
00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:24,577
I'm hardly well known, but
I make enough to survive.

47
00:03:24,660 --> 00:03:26,657
Explain how you became a stand user.

48
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:30,317
I'm sorry, but I don't know what
any of those words even mean.

49
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:32,157
If you're referring to this power,

50
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:35,181
it just sort of appeared
one day when I was a kid.

51
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:36,777
Was it the same for you?

52
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:37,690
Hey, quiet!

53
00:03:37,773 --> 00:03:39,097
I got a lot more to ask.

54
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:42,237
Why the hell did you follow me
all the way from the restaurant?

55
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:45,614
And how does some randu like
you know who Bucciarati is?

56
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:47,350
Bucciarati?

57
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:49,977
Does that happen to be his name by chance?

58
00:03:50,060 --> 00:03:50,920
Please, hurry!

59
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:52,416
Bring him to me now!

60
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,588
You haven't answered any of my
questions, you son of a bitch!

61
00:03:59,440 --> 00:04:02,257
I'm afraid you're not going
to like what I have to say.

62
00:04:02,340 --> 00:04:03,700
I can't control it.

63
00:04:03,980 --> 00:04:06,215
The rock has its own independent will.

64
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:08,677
It's always been that
way, as far as I'm aware.

65
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:11,936
Unfortunately, there's nothing
I can do to rein it in.

66
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:15,512
However, you are not the person it wants.

67
00:04:16,180 --> 00:04:19,060
Right now, the rock is
seeking out Bucciarati.

68
00:04:19,340 --> 00:04:20,240
Oh, really?

69
00:04:20,460 --> 00:04:21,837
Do I look stupid to you?

70
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:24,417
You better get serious about
this right freaking now,

71
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:26,997
unless you never want to
pick up a chisel ever again.

72
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:30,837
I know Bucciarati's nowhere near this
place, so quit trying to fool me,

73
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:32,937
because I can hurt you a lot worse.

74
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:35,196
You're the only one fooling yourself.

75
00:04:35,660 --> 00:04:37,877
Bucciarati is without a
doubt inside this building.

76
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:39,997
Once again, I'm begging
you to let me see him.

77
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:41,677
His life is in grave danger!

78
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:43,437
What did I say about lying to me?!

79
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:45,517
Don't test my patience, you murderer!

80
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:47,894
I should end you for killing that girl!

81
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:59,877
What the hell are you
plotting now, asshole?!

82
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:02,897
Which part of Don't Try Anything
Funny wasn't clear to you?!

83
00:05:02,980 --> 00:05:04,417
It's left...

84
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:06,060
It wants nothing from us.

85
00:05:06,700 --> 00:05:07,530
What?!

86
00:05:08,180 --> 00:05:10,239
Allow me to share some art history.

87
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:12,780
The sculptor Michelangelo once said,

88
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:17,660
I approach the marble with chisel in
hand, but with no thought in my mind.

89
00:05:18,780 --> 00:05:22,660
For the stone already knows well
the form it is destined to take.

90
00:05:23,220 --> 00:05:24,400
And to that end,

91
00:05:24,640 --> 00:05:29,140
my hands are tools, made simply to
deliver the medium, but never shape it.

92
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:31,137
Laurie, that's enough, you goddamn nerd!

93
00:05:31,220 --> 00:05:33,957
I'm gonna need you to bring that
stupid rock back here right now,

94
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:35,357
or I'll shoot you dead!

95
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:37,852
A sculpture's ultimate form is not given.

96
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:39,988
Michelangelo would conject.

97
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:44,159
The sculptor's only job was to
unearth what fate had already created.

98
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:48,417
He could see fate's design growing
clearer with each strike of his chisel.

99
00:05:48,500 --> 00:05:49,980
Do you understand now?

100
00:05:50,380 --> 00:05:52,968
I did not give the stone
Bucciarati's shape.

101
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:54,591
Neither did your bullets.

102
00:05:55,260 --> 00:05:57,100
It was solely fate's doing.

103
00:05:57,940 --> 00:06:01,646
I'm guessing you saw the massive
chest wound and gush of blood.

104
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:05,312
Whether it will be in days or
months, none can really say.

105
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:09,280
But it is the way in which
Bucciarati will meet his end.

106
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:13,245
You and I are nothing
more than slaves to fate.

107
00:06:13,580 --> 00:06:15,992
That is the significance behind my power.

108
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:17,261
Prophecy Stones.

109
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:20,157
This is the last warning I'll give you.

110
00:06:20,240 --> 00:06:21,997
Bring that damn rock back now!

111
00:06:22,080 --> 00:06:25,137
Because if your dumbass eats it,
then so does your little Stan.

112
00:06:25,220 --> 00:06:26,697
Do you get what I'm saying?

113
00:06:26,780 --> 00:06:28,697
If he touches my Prophecy Stones,

114
00:06:28,780 --> 00:06:32,317
I promise he'll be granted a
merciful release with no suffering.

115
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:35,580
So please, I only wish
to hear his last words.

116
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:37,140
Let me be by his side.

117
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:39,301
What the hell is this guy's deal?

118
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:41,157
Is he mocking me or something?

119
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:44,122
The bastard hasn't flinched
once this whole time!

120
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:45,150
Okay, fine.

121
00:06:45,233 --> 00:06:48,777
If you seriously want me to spray the
place with your insides, then wish granted,

122
00:06:48,860 --> 00:06:49,690
pal!

123
00:06:49,773 --> 00:06:52,874
I got three whole bullets
while you just have one brain!

124
00:06:54,660 --> 00:06:57,954
Let's take a look at what
fate buried in your mushy ass!

125
00:07:00,400 --> 00:07:04,237
I know you're trying to do something
weird to Bucciarati, so stop playing dumb!

126
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:06,026
Call your freaking rock back!

127
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:09,857
Trust me, friend, you really don't want
to test how much time you got left!

128
00:07:09,940 --> 00:07:13,940
As I said, at this point there's
not a single thing more to be done.

129
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:19,592
Cut the bullshit act and bring
the rock back, you bastard!

130
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:24,600
The florist who sent you, his
legs were no good, were they?

131
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:27,513
He doesn't know it yet.

132
00:07:27,660 --> 00:07:32,080
but it's an early symptom of some
organ disease, one he won't overcome.

133
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:34,400
At least not on his own.

134
00:07:34,880 --> 00:07:36,704
Soon after the daughter passed,

135
00:07:36,860 --> 00:07:39,557
her healthy organs were
preserved for transplantation

136
00:07:39,640 --> 00:07:41,993
and will eventually save the man's life.

137
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:45,077
Poor girl found out about
her father's ailment

138
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:47,857
from the rock and learned
that in a few months,

139
00:07:47,940 --> 00:07:49,764
she'd contract the disease too.

140
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:52,937
It was a revelation she accepted.

141
00:07:53,020 --> 00:07:57,860
She chose death to save her father
and to avoid suffering later.

142
00:07:58,360 --> 00:08:00,948
That's the reason why
she embraced the rock.

143
00:08:05,520 --> 00:08:08,737
She was freed from the dark
fate awaiting her and granted

144
00:08:08,820 --> 00:08:12,173
a merciful death which would
leave all her organs intact.

145
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:18,171
That's a pretty messed up way of saying
you killed an innocent girl, psycho!

146
00:08:19,660 --> 00:08:20,637
What the...?

147
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:21,837
It's a misfire!

148
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:23,861
Looks like that bullet was a dud.

149
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:25,710
Really?

150
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:30,035
Hey, that bullet was supposed to be
stupid number five's responsibility.

151
00:08:30,540 --> 00:08:31,370
Get it?

152
00:08:31,540 --> 00:08:32,960
It's not my time yet.

153
00:08:34,040 --> 00:08:36,981
My death still hasn't found
its form in the stone.

154
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:39,537
If you really think I'm going
to shoot two blanks in a row,

155
00:08:39,620 --> 00:08:41,837
then you've lost your tiny little mind.

156
00:08:41,920 --> 00:08:45,040
What you felt just now
was destiny nudging you.

157
00:08:45,820 --> 00:08:49,260
You've lost any real desire
to shoot me. Isn't that right?

158
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:59,057
You've got to be kidding me
with all this Destiny bullshit.

159
00:08:59,140 --> 00:09:01,937
There's no way any of that
made-up nonsense is real.

160
00:09:02,020 --> 00:09:03,491
That bastard's just nuts.

161
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:06,120
Come on, come on.

162
00:09:06,220 --> 00:09:07,177
Are you there, Fugo?

163
00:09:07,260 --> 00:09:09,117
I got some news on our sculptor friend.

164
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:12,360
As it turns out, the guy's
a stand user. Wait, what?

165
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:16,877
Yeah, the weirdo won't shut up about
Bucciarati and Destiny and whatnot.

166
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:19,557
I can't make sense of anything
he's been babbling about.

167
00:09:19,640 --> 00:09:20,877
I'd say the same about you.

168
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:22,560
Isn't Bucciarati there?

169
00:09:23,020 --> 00:09:26,977
He got out of the car right after you and
headed straight to the apartment building.

170
00:09:27,060 --> 00:09:29,697
I thought for sure he would have
caught up with you at this point.

171
00:09:29,780 --> 00:09:32,360
Give me a break! What's going on?

172
00:09:45,180 --> 00:09:46,220
Hey, Fugo!

173
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:49,037
Can you remember what the number
to Bucciarati's phone was?

174
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:51,717
It's really important that I
get to him right the hell now.

175
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:55,800
Whoa, hey breathe the phone you're
calling is Bucciarati's you moron

176
00:09:57,580 --> 00:09:59,560
Hey Mista, you listening?

177
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:05,080
I'm counting on you guys
find Bucciarati quick.

178
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:06,110
Hello

179
00:10:06,860 --> 00:10:09,040
All right princess nap time's over.

180
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:12,593
Tell me how to stop this damn
rock from killing my friend

181
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:13,630
Hey,

182
00:10:13,713 --> 00:10:18,477
I told you to wake up you answer me
right freaking now Tell me exactly

183
00:10:18,560 --> 00:10:22,972
what I gotta do to stop that dumb pebble
of yours from reaching Bucciarati!

184
00:10:27,260 --> 00:10:28,757
Come on, man, I'm begging you.

185
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:30,605
Please help me save my friend.

186
00:10:31,140 --> 00:10:34,552
Look, I think I'm starting to
get all that stuff you said,

187
00:10:34,820 --> 00:10:37,820
but you gotta tell me how
to turn this ship around.

188
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:40,397
Bucciarati is not touching that rock.

189
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:41,892
I can't let that happen.

190
00:10:43,040 --> 00:10:45,537
So please, what's the secret?

191
00:10:45,620 --> 00:10:47,000
You gotta tell me!

192
00:10:48,040 --> 00:10:49,960
I suggest you do not resist.

193
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:52,925
Acceptance is the easier path.

194
00:10:53,900 --> 00:10:58,080
Still, if you're set on defying
the rock, there might be a way.

195
00:10:59,100 --> 00:11:02,997
If you can destroy it or reshape
it somehow, then maybe...

196
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:04,340
We found him, mister!

197
00:11:04,700 --> 00:11:06,320
We got eyes on Bucciarati!

198
00:11:06,560 --> 00:11:09,197
A report came in from Number
One confirming it's him!

199
00:11:09,280 --> 00:11:11,637
Bucciarati is somewhere
on the seventh floor!

200
00:11:11,720 --> 00:11:12,820
Wait, I got it!

201
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:13,957
It's the stairwell!

202
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:15,511
He's climbing the stairs!

203
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:17,660
Oh, shit! No!

204
00:11:18,660 --> 00:11:19,940
Not good, not good!

205
00:11:20,620 --> 00:11:21,800
I see the rock!

206
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:23,060
It beat us to him!

207
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:25,120
Holy crap, what do we do?

208
00:11:25,300 --> 00:11:26,280
He's gonna die!

209
00:11:26,940 --> 00:11:28,397
Get it together, Number One!

210
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:31,417
Just focus on getting there
and tell him not to touch it!

211
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:32,330
It's no use!

212
00:11:32,413 --> 00:11:34,517
Number One's bullet doesn't
have nearly enough juice

213
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:37,424
left in it to get him all
the way there in time!

214
00:11:39,980 --> 00:11:40,810
Bucciarati!

215
00:11:42,700 --> 00:11:43,660
Yee-haw!

216
00:11:53,760 --> 00:11:54,800
Six bullets.

217
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:56,440
We made it!

218
00:11:56,620 --> 00:11:57,540
That was close.

219
00:11:57,840 --> 00:12:00,080
And it looks like we did to the thing.

220
00:12:14,020 --> 00:12:16,877
I mean, it's cool that we've
got it crumbling and everything,

221
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:20,377
but I think we might have just
made stuff a whole lot worse.

222
00:12:20,460 --> 00:12:23,357
Hey, bullets, why don't you fill
me in on what's going on here?

223
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:25,087
Are we dealing with a stand?

224
00:12:26,540 --> 00:12:29,997
And can any of you explain why
the hell it looks like that?

225
00:12:30,080 --> 00:12:32,374
Oh no, Mujirachi, get away from it now!

226
00:12:32,540 --> 00:12:33,560
Zipperman, go!

227
00:12:34,220 --> 00:12:36,240
No, don't go, Zipperman!

228
00:12:36,700 --> 00:12:38,347
If you touch it, you'll die!

229
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:43,206
Get down from there, quickly!

230
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:46,917
Mister, trust me, you're not gonna
wanna lay a finger on that rock.

231
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,882
One small tap and it's all over.

232
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:50,277
Explain yourself.

233
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:52,889
I'll do that as soon
as we get out of here!

234
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:57,551
Is that stone mass supposed to be a stand?

235
00:12:57,720 --> 00:13:02,249
Please stop asking me all these questions
and run away for your life already?

236
00:13:02,460 --> 00:13:05,872
Crap, it's slipping away again,
just like in the elevator.

237
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:14,560
Damn it, that thing could
attack at any moment.

238
00:13:14,820 --> 00:13:16,797
We'll need to find another way to get out.

239
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:19,557
This stairwell just turned
into a goddamn death trap.

240
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:22,287
Let's stay on our toes
and climb out of here.

241
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:25,220
Where is it?

242
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:28,340
I hate that slippery little bastard.

243
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:29,960
Where did it go?

244
00:13:31,280 --> 00:13:33,760
Mista, what is it you've learned?

245
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:37,680
Clever son of a bitch!

246
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:38,837
It's right above you!

247
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:39,750
Look out!

248
00:13:47,180 --> 00:13:49,540
Why does this rock bear that face?

249
00:13:58,420 --> 00:14:00,740
I just need to destroy the rock.

250
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:03,860
Or at least try to
change its shape somehow.

251
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:05,390
Mista!

252
00:14:05,520 --> 00:14:08,157
If I smash it into the
pavement from this high,

253
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:11,122
that should be enough to
shatter its ass to bits!

254
00:14:12,060 --> 00:14:13,920
I don't think so!

255
00:14:16,620 --> 00:14:18,540
Oh no! Mista!

256
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:33,537
holy shit he was telling the truth

257
00:14:33,620 --> 00:14:38,000
after all everything went just as he said

258
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:41,617
as long as you don't
see your own mug carved

259
00:14:41,700 --> 00:14:44,737
inside the stone you get
to live on for at least

260
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:48,757
another day nice what
the hell were you doing

261
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:53,100
in there mister you left
the recorder in the car

262
00:14:53,740 --> 00:14:55,328
after your tantrum, doofus.

263
00:14:55,680 --> 00:14:56,520
Oh, hey.

264
00:14:57,020 --> 00:14:58,180
It's you, Fugo.

265
00:15:05,660 --> 00:15:07,920
So what on earth were you in the end?

266
00:15:09,020 --> 00:15:12,432
Mista, I'd very much like the
explanation you promised me.

267
00:15:13,260 --> 00:15:15,360
I mean, none of it matters anymore.

268
00:15:15,840 --> 00:15:19,760
I wouldn't know where to
begin, even. Oh, wait.

269
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:21,901
How about the old man's daughter?

270
00:15:22,320 --> 00:15:24,140
It's the boyfriend, I'd say.

271
00:15:25,660 --> 00:15:28,140
But technically, it also wasn't him.

272
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:34,737
Either way, he's not leaving the
hospital for at least a few months, so...

273
00:15:34,820 --> 00:15:37,440
Unhelpfully vague as ever. Classic.

274
00:15:38,580 --> 00:15:39,720
Is he a friend?

275
00:15:39,860 --> 00:15:41,240
Or do we kick his ass?

276
00:15:41,520 --> 00:15:43,100
Also, was it suicide?

277
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:45,477
Why don't you start from the beginning?

278
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:47,560
But see, that's the thing, though.

279
00:15:47,700 --> 00:15:50,260
It's really hard to, you know,

280
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:53,497
piece this whole thing together
in a way that makes sense.

281
00:15:53,580 --> 00:15:57,377
Look, all you need to know is that
I destroyed the mean old rock stand,

282
00:15:57,460 --> 00:15:59,080
so everything's peachy now.

283
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:06,997
Oh yeah, how's about you let me take
over the whole leaky eye Luca thing?

284
00:16:07,080 --> 00:16:09,500
No thanks, I've decided to do it myself.

285
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:11,997
Your reporting skills would slow things.

286
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:14,315
I believe I'll do just fine on my own.

287
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:18,480
Fugo, our florist friend
should get a detailed account.

288
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:20,724
Gather what you can from Mista.

289
00:16:21,260 --> 00:16:24,480
Bucciarati, you know you
have my utmost respect.

290
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:28,200
But this guy here, he's a
puzzle even I can't solve.

291
00:16:32,060 --> 00:16:33,640
Okay, don't hurt yourself.

292
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:36,200
We'll just have to use Abakio's...

293
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:40,180
So naive, do you really
believe this is the end?

294
00:16:41,060 --> 00:16:43,840
If only you had accepted
the stone's mercy.

295
00:16:44,260 --> 00:16:45,720
All would be peaceful.

296
00:16:46,980 --> 00:16:49,960
But you chose to remain enslaved to fate.

297
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:53,940
That which is carved in
stone cannot be changed.

298
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:57,380
Whoever you are, I hope you're ready.

299
00:16:57,720 --> 00:17:00,240
A perilous journey of hardship awaits.

300
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:04,000
And for some of you, it
will be the last one.

301
00:17:05,540 --> 00:17:08,460
I wonder, are all of you like him?

302
00:17:09,760 --> 00:17:12,840
That young man flung
himself off a tall building.

303
00:17:13,540 --> 00:17:15,658
All for a chance to save his friend.

304
00:17:16,900 --> 00:17:21,700
Perhaps the path you are bound to walk
isn't one of meaningless suffering.

305
00:17:22,160 --> 00:17:26,520
The adversity you'll endure may well
be the crucible of hope for another.

306
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:30,640
And perhaps it could be the
birth of a greater purpose.

307
00:17:32,620 --> 00:17:35,032
Wishing for their safety will do nothing.

308
00:17:35,260 --> 00:17:38,140
I can only hope that
they are sleeping slaves.

309
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:39,630
That's it.

310
00:17:40,520 --> 00:17:45,740
Sleeping slaves will eventually awaken to
discover some meaning in their suffering.

311
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:54,937
Hey, what's the hold up?

312
00:17:55,020 --> 00:17:56,717
Do you want me to heal Bucciarati?

313
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:59,682
Sure, why didn't I just
rub my gun on his wounds?

314
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:02,572
Dude, are you listening?

315
00:18:04,060 --> 00:18:06,295
Whoa there, you gotta watch your step.

316
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:07,230
Thanks, Mista.

317
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:09,575
Something really weird just popped up.

318
00:18:19,740 --> 00:18:20,570
Trish?

319
00:18:21,180 --> 00:18:22,520
Hey, Trish!

320
00:18:23,800 --> 00:18:24,720
Where'd you go?

321
00:18:25,280 --> 00:18:26,110
Trish!

322
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:27,260
Hey, Giorno!

323
00:18:27,420 --> 00:18:29,057
Where the hell did that girl go?

324
00:18:29,140 --> 00:18:30,140
You startled me.

325
00:18:30,700 --> 00:18:32,920
She's right there behind you. Look.

326
00:18:34,700 --> 00:18:36,900
Guys, it's alright. I'm here.

327
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:39,937
The thing I tripped on
was next to the rock.

328
00:18:40,020 --> 00:18:40,850
Check it out.

329
00:18:40,940 --> 00:18:42,764
Don't go leaving me behind now.

330
00:18:43,260 --> 00:18:45,025
Sorry I gave you all a fright.

331
00:18:45,180 --> 00:18:47,197
I hope you'll still take me with you.

332
00:18:47,280 --> 00:18:49,280
It's a long way for a lone turtle.

333
00:18:49,840 --> 00:18:51,017
Why are you still here?

334
00:18:51,100 --> 00:18:51,930
It's Mr.

335
00:18:52,013 --> 00:18:52,843
Polnareff.

336
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:55,620
How are you alive?

337
00:18:56,360 --> 00:19:00,197
If our souls were switched back to normal,
doesn't that mean yours should be...

338
00:19:00,280 --> 00:19:01,917
Wait a minute, that's not right.

339
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:03,377
Wouldn't you...

340
00:19:03,460 --> 00:19:04,340
And that?

341
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:06,660
My original body has perished.

342
00:19:06,900 --> 00:19:09,480
But the moment my spirit
departed my flesh,

343
00:19:09,700 --> 00:19:12,897
I made sure to hang on as tight
as I could to this turtle.

344
00:19:12,980 --> 00:19:15,392
I'll remain bound to this key for a time.

345
00:19:15,540 --> 00:19:19,011
I hope you won't mind little
old spectral me tagging along.

346
00:19:20,300 --> 00:19:23,437
Hot damn, I'll admit I'm glad to
see you're still kicking and stuff,

347
00:19:23,520 --> 00:19:25,108
but the day's not over yet.

348
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:28,097
We still need to patch
out Bucciarati's injuries.

349
00:19:28,180 --> 00:19:29,400
Wait, Bucciarati?

350
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:31,900
But I thought his soul was...

351
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:43,937
Whoa, what are you doing?

352
00:19:44,020 --> 00:19:45,320
Oh, crap, my bad.

353
00:19:45,780 --> 00:19:48,257
I was just thinking maybe
you might have had a point.

354
00:19:48,340 --> 00:19:50,780
My pits, they actually do smell like ass.

355
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:53,997
Can't believe I'm just
now learning about this.

356
00:19:54,080 --> 00:19:56,137
Maybe I should put on clone after all.

357
00:19:56,220 --> 00:19:57,050
What?

358
00:19:58,480 --> 00:20:01,357
Look, I might have exaggerated
a little bit earlier.

359
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:02,897
Everything happens so fast.

360
00:20:02,980 --> 00:20:04,677
Right now, I don't think
you smell that bad.

361
00:20:04,760 --> 00:20:08,172
In a super weird kind of way,
it actually feels nostalgic.

362
00:20:08,960 --> 00:20:11,540
Oh my gosh, do you really mean that?

363
00:20:12,300 --> 00:20:14,418
Yeah, but your fingers are freakish.

364
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:23,240
So then, what's your choice?

365
00:20:24,800 --> 00:20:28,017
When those who've left us
place their wills in our hands,

366
00:20:28,100 --> 00:20:30,820
it is our sacred duty to carry it forth.

367
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:33,740
It remains.

368
00:20:34,240 --> 00:20:35,400
That's my choice.

369
00:20:37,560 --> 00:20:40,089
Why don't you keep the
arrow in the turtle?

370
00:20:41,460 --> 00:20:43,060
That'll do, Giorno.

371
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:48,620
A worthy decision to fulfill
your duty as a survivor.

372
00:20:56,980 --> 00:21:01,340
Let us go to the Coliseum.

373
00:21:18,620 --> 00:21:22,160
What is just fiction or what is the truth?

374
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:24,297
They have the mission,

375
00:21:24,380 --> 00:21:30,520
they are the passion But they dare
to tell us what's bad and what's good

376
00:21:31,500 --> 00:21:35,940
Stand up, join us Come on,

377
00:21:36,180 --> 00:21:42,060
I'll say this a lot We are
the power who sees the future

378
00:21:42,840 --> 00:21:48,060
Cause we are the fighters
She's falling for a ride
